    weborg: browser org-mode clone with vim bindings
    
    Static, backend-free org-mode subset: heading folding, TODO state
    cycling, tags, priorities, DEADLINE/SCHEDULED with a vim-navigable
    calendar popup, agenda view, minibuffer commands, localStorage
    persistence, .org import/export. Vim-style keymap (hjkl, operators,
    counts, insert mode with jk-Esc, arrow keys supported).
    
    47 tests: 16 core (pure node) + 31 DOM integration (jsdom).
    
    app: drop no-op = binding, close prompt before help overlay, doc-meta stats
    
    org-native bindings: M-arrow/M-hjkl section moves, typed dates, text-first visuals
    
    - M-up/down (M-k/j) move section among siblings; M-left/right (M-h/l)
      promote/demote; M-RET new sibling heading -- all capture-phase so
      browser back/forward can't intercept. Model ops live in org.js and
      are unit-tested.
    - Calendar popup removed; deadline/scheduled are now typed in the
      minibuffer (YYYY-MM-DD, DD.MM[.YYYY], today, +3d, -1w, empty clears).
      parseDateInput moved to org.js; parseDate now rejects rolled-over
      invalid dates (e.g. Feb 30).
    - Tags render inline as :a:b: instead of pills; kw badges became plain
      colored text; dropped all rounded corners/shadows/popup CSS.
    - storage probe: works over file:// where localStorage is blocked.
    - README rewritten for the zero-dependency story.
    
    drop jsdom test harness and npm scaffolding
    
    plain-text editing, normal-mode cursor, h/l movement, help wrap
    
    - i on a heading edits the whole org line as text: TODO keyword,
      [#A] priority and :tags: are typed inline and re-parsed on commit
    - new 'a' binding (insert after caret), 0 jumps to column 0
    - visible block cursor in normal mode (accent-colored char at caret)
